# Lab 20: Companion registration rename experiment
#
# Question:
# When an approved disposable GCP agent is renamed, does Registry Sync retain
# the exact provider sourceAgentId, and can every in-scope Agent 365 display
# name be synchronized without replacing any object or changing any ID?
#
# Run one request at a time. Never use "Send All".
#
# The evidence path is read-only:
#   Part 1 -> manually rename the disposable GCP agent -> Part 2 -> Stop A
#
# Parts 3 through 6 are one-variable-at-a-time name synchronization writes.
# Do not send them until Stop A confirms that the scoped provider source key
# is unchanged. A changed sourceAgentId is not an in-place rename.
#
# Put all real values in the shared ignored ../../.env file:
#
# A365_TENANT_ID=<directory-tenant-id>
# A365_CLIENT_ID=<public-client-application-id>
# A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME=<display-name-before-provider-rename>
# A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-before-provider-rename>
# A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-source-id-before-provider-rename>
# A365_DEMO_ASSIGNMENT_MODE=<dedicated-or-shared>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP=<mapped-assignment-group>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID=<mapped-blueprint-object-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID=<mapped-blueprint-app-id>
# A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID=<mapped-blueprint-principal-id>
# A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID=<existing-agent-identity-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID=<exact-mapped-companion-source-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID=<existing-companion-registration-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH=<path-safe-registration-id>
# A365_DEMO_COMPANION_PACKAGE_ID=<existing-companion-package-id>
# A365_RENAME_NEW_TARGET_NAME=<display-name-after-provider-rename>
# A365_RENAME_AFTER_PACKAGE_ID=<package-id-observed-after-sync>
# A365_RENAME_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT=<exact-source-modified-timestamp-after-sync>
#
# Preserve the before and after sourceAgentId values byte-for-byte in ignored
# evidence. Do not URL-decode, normalize, or put them in tracked files.
#
# Save private responses only under:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/

@tenantId = {{$dotenv A365_TENANT_ID}}
@clientId = {{$dotenv A365_CLIENT_ID}}
@oldTargetName = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_TARGET_NAME}}
@originalPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ORIGINAL_PACKAGE_ID}}
@expectedSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@assignmentMode = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_ASSIGNMENT_MODE}}
@blueprintGroup = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_GROUP}}
@blueprintObjectId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_OBJECT_ID}}
@blueprintAppId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID}}
@blueprintPrincipalId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID}}
@agentIdentityId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID}}
@companionSourceAgentId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID}}
@companionRegistrationId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID}}
@companionRegistrationIdPath = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID_PATH}}
@companionPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_DEMO_COMPANION_PACKAGE_ID}}
@newTargetName = {{$dotenv A365_RENAME_NEW_TARGET_NAME}}
@afterPackageId = {{$dotenv A365_RENAME_AFTER_PACKAGE_ID}}
@newSourceModifiedAt = {{$dotenv A365_RENAME_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT}}
@graphBaseUrl = https://graph.microsoft.com
@renameScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FCopilotPackages.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprint.UpdateBranding.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentIdentity.ReadWrite.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.Read.All%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FAgentRegistration.ReadWrite.All%20offline_access
@principalRenameScopes = https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FUser.Read%20https%3A%2F%2Fgraph.microsoft.com%2FApplication.ReadWrite.All%20offline_access

###############################################################################
# Authentication 1 - Request a device code
#
# Never save this response.

# @name renameStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{renameScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Authentication 2 - Exchange the device code after browser sign-in
#
# Never save this response.

# @name renameToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{renameStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 1.1 - Confirm the signed-in operator
#
# Send after Authentication 2 succeeds. Expected: 200.
# Keep the returned user ID private.

# @name renameCurrentUser
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/me?$select=id
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.1
#
# Do not save this response. The operator ID is used only by the live session.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.2 - Capture Package inventory before the provider rename
#
# Expected: 200. Read every returned page before continuing. Locate the
# original Registry Sync Package by platform, provider scope, and exact nested
# sourceAgentId rather than display name alone.

# @name renameListPackagesBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.2
#
# 1. Save the first page:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/package-list-before-provider-rename-page-1.json
# 2. If @odata.nextLink exists, save every additional page as
#    package-list-before-provider-rename-page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.

###############################################################################
# Part 1.3 - Capture the original Package before the provider rename
#
# Expected: 200.
# Record privately:
# - Package ID
# - displayName
# - platform
# - connection/provenance metadata
# - exact nested provider sourceAgentId
# - provider scope
# - source-created and source-modified timestamps

# @name renameGetPackageBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{originalPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.3
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/original-package-before-provider-rename.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.4 - Verify the mapped Blueprint
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm its object ID and appId match the locked assignment.

# @name renameGetBlueprintBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.4
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-before-rename.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.5 - Verify the enabled Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 200. Confirm id equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_PRINCIPAL_ID, appId
# equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID, and accountEnabled is not false.

# @name renameGetBlueprintPrincipalBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.5
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-principal-before-rename.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.6 - Capture the existing Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 200. Record only field presence and safe comparison results in
# tracked notes.

# @name renameGetIdentityBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.6
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/agent-identity-before-rename.json

###############################################################################
# Part 1.7 - Capture the existing companion Registration
#
# Expected: 200.
# Confirm:
# - the ID is A365_DEMO_COMPANION_REGISTRATION_ID
# - sourceAgentId equals A365_DEMO_COMPANION_SOURCE_AGENT_ID exactly
# - new mappings use agent-governance:companion:v1:gcp:<provider-source-id>
# - preserve a mapped legacy value rather than changing identity during rename
# - agentIdentityBlueprintId equals A365_DEMO_BLUEPRINT_APP_ID
# - agentIdentityId equals A365_DEMO_AGENT_IDENTITY_ID

# @name renameGetRegistrationBefore
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationIdPath}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 1.7
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/companion-registration-before-rename.json

###############################################################################
# Manual provider checkpoint - no request
#
# Only with explicit approval, rename the existing disposable GCP agent in its
# supported provider administration interface. Do not delete or recreate it.
#
# Wait for a successful Registry Sync cycle and the agreed propagation period.
# Then set:
#
# A365_RENAME_NEW_TARGET_NAME=<new-provider-display-name>
#
# Do not change A365_DEMO_PROVIDER_SOURCE_AGENT_ID. It is the before value used
# for byte-for-byte comparison.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.1 - Read Package inventory after provider rename and sync
#
# Expected: 200. Read every page.
#
# Find the Package carrying the new display name, then identify it using its
# platform, provider scope, and exact nested sourceAgentId. Put its observed
# Package ID into A365_RENAME_AFTER_PACKAGE_ID.

# @name renameListPackagesAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.1
#
# 1. Save the first page:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/package-list-after-provider-rename-page-1.json
# 2. If @odata.nextLink exists, save every additional page as
#    package-list-after-provider-rename-page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.
# 3. Set A365_RENAME_AFTER_PACKAGE_ID only after locating exactly one Package
#    with the expected platform, provider scope, and unchanged sourceAgentId.

###############################################################################
# Part 2.2 - Read the selected Package after provider rename and sync
#
# Expected: 200 after A365_RENAME_AFTER_PACKAGE_ID is set.
# Copy the exact nested LastModifiedDateTime into
# A365_RENAME_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT before any PATCH.

# @name renameGetPackageAfter
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{afterPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 2.2
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/provider-package-after-rename.json
#
# Copy the exact nested LastModifiedDateTime into
# A365_RENAME_SOURCE_MODIFIED_AT before continuing to Stop A.

###############################################################################
# Stop A - classify before sending any PATCH
#
# Compare Part 1.3 and Part 2.2 byte-for-byte:
#
# A. Same sourceAgentId and same provider scope:
#    This is an in-place rename candidate. The Package ID may be unchanged or
#    replaced; update only the Package ID in the durable mapping if needed.
#
# B. Different sourceAgentId or provider scope:
#    Stop. Record reconciliation-required. Do not PATCH, POST, or DELETE any
#    companion object. This may be a source migration or delete plus add.
#
# C. Old and new Packages both remain:
#    Stop. Allow more sync time and investigate duplication.
#
# D. No renamed Package is visible:
#    Stop. The result is unavailable or inconclusive, not deletion.
#
# Continue only for case A and only after confirming that the saved
# companion Registration and Agent Identity still belong to this source.

###############################################################################
# Mapping checkpoint - record the observed provider rename
#
# Run from the Lab 20 directory:
#
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py
#
# This writes mapping-after-rename.json with the observed display name of each
# object. For the current rename, nameSyncStatus should be pending. Re-run the
# same command after every verified GET below; it advances to in-sync only
# when every object covered by the assignment policy has its expected name.
#
# The mapping records these independent observations:
# - packageDisplayName
# - blueprintDisplayName
# - blueprintPrincipalDisplayName
# - agentIdentityDisplayName
# - companionRegistrationDisplayName
# - companionPackageDisplayName
# - nameSyncStatus

###############################################################################
# Part 3 - Synchronize the Blueprint names
#
# Dedicated example:
#   GCP Agent A owns its own Blueprint, so the Blueprint name follows Agent A.
#
# Shared example:
#   Agents A and B use "Support Team Blueprint", so neither agent may rename
#   the shared Blueprint or principal. Skip Part 3 and continue to Part 4.

###############################################################################
# Part 3.1 - Rename the dedicated Blueprint
#
# Send only when A365_DEMO_ASSIGNMENT_MODE is dedicated and the mapped
# Blueprint is used only by this provider source. Do not send for shared mode.
#
# If Authentication 1 and 2 were completed before this file added
# AgentIdentityBlueprint.UpdateBranding.All, request a fresh device code and
# token. Stop rather than approving unexpected tenant-wide consent.
#
# Expected: 204. This changes only the Blueprint displayName.

# @name renamePatchBlueprint
PATCH {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "{{newTargetName}} - dedicated disposable Blueprint"
}

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 3.1
#
# A successful 204 has no JSON response body. Do not create a fake JSON
# response file. Continue immediately to Part 3.2.

###############################################################################
# Part 3.2 - Verify the dedicated Blueprint rename
#
# Expected: 200 with the same object ID and appId and the new displayName.

# @name renameGetBlueprintAfterNameSync
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/applications/{{blueprintObjectId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprint
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 3.2
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-after-name-sync.json
#
# Confirm the object ID and appId match blueprint-before-rename.json. Then run:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py

###############################################################################
# Part 3.3 - Observe whether the Blueprint principal followed automatically
#
# Expected: 200 with the same principal ID and appId. This observation answers
# whether changing the Blueprint also updates its tenant principal.

# @name renameGetBlueprintPrincipalAfterBlueprint
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 3.3
#
# If the principal already has the new Blueprint name, save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-principal-after-name-sync.json
#
# Then run prepare_rename.py and skip Parts 3.4 through 3.7.
#
# If it still has the old name, save instead:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-principal-after-blueprint-rename.json
# and continue to Stop B.

###############################################################################
# Stop B - separately approve a Blueprint principal rename
#
# The documented general service-principal update requires
# Application.ReadWrite.All. That broader permission is intentionally absent
# from the normal rename token.
#
# Stop with nameSyncStatus=blocked unless all of the following are true:
# - the principal did not follow the Blueprint automatically;
# - the assignment is dedicated;
# - this exact principal update is explicitly approved;
# - the public client and operator are already authorized for the broader
#   permission; and
# - browser sign-in does not request new tenant consent.
#
# Parts 3.4 through 3.7 are an optional bounded experiment, not the default
# committed-fleet path.
#
# When the principal name is required by policy but this branch cannot safely
# run, record the boundary:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py --blocked

###############################################################################
# Part 3.4 - OPTIONAL request a separate principal-write device code
#
# Never save this response. Stop if sign-in asks for new tenant consent.

# @name renamePrincipalStartDeviceCode
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/devicecode
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id={{clientId}}&scope={{principalRenameScopes}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.5 - OPTIONAL exchange the principal-write device code
#
# Never save this response.

# @name renamePrincipalToken
POST https://login.microsoftonline.com/{{tenantId}}/oauth2/v2.0/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=urn%3Aietf%3Aparams%3Aoauth%3Agrant-type%3Adevice_code&client_id={{clientId}}&device_code={{renamePrincipalStartDeviceCode.response.body.$.device_code}}

###

###############################################################################
# Part 3.6 - OPTIONAL rename the dedicated Blueprint principal
#
# Expected: 204. Change only displayName and identify the derived type.

# @name renamePatchBlueprintPrincipal
PATCH {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{blueprintPrincipalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renamePrincipalToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "@odata.type": "#microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal",
  "displayName": "{{newTargetName}} - dedicated disposable Blueprint"
}

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 3.6
#
# A successful 204 has no JSON response body. Do not create a fake JSON
# response file. Continue immediately to Part 3.7.

###############################################################################
# Part 3.7 - Verify the Blueprint principal rename
#
# Expected: 200 with unchanged ID and appId and the new displayName.

# @name renameGetBlueprintPrincipalAfterNameSync
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals(appId='{{blueprintAppId}}')/microsoft.graph.agentIdentityBlueprintPrincipal
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 3.7
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/blueprint-principal-after-name-sync.json
#
# Run:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py

###############################################################################
# Part 4.1 - Rename the existing Agent Identity
#
# Expected: 204. This changes display metadata only; the Identity ID and
# Blueprint relationship must remain unchanged.

# @name renamePatchIdentity
PATCH {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "displayName": "{{newTargetName}} - managed Agent Identity"
}

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 4.1
#
# A successful 204 has no JSON response body. Do not create a fake JSON file.

###############################################################################
# Part 4.2 - Verify the Agent Identity rename
#
# Expected: 200 with the same ID and Blueprint appId and the new displayName.

# @name renameGetIdentityAfterNameSync
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/servicePrincipals/{{agentIdentityId}}/microsoft.graph.agentIdentity
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 4.2
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/agent-identity-after-name-sync.json
#
# Confirm the ID and Blueprint appId are unchanged. Then run:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py

###############################################################################
# Part 5.1 - Rename the existing companion Registration
#
# Expected: 200 with an empty response body.
#
# Do not PATCH sourceAgentId, originatingStore, Blueprint, identity, or owner.
# Carry the exact newly observed provider source-modified timestamp.

# @name renamePatchRegistration
PATCH {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationIdPath}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

{
  "displayName": "{{newTargetName}} - managed companion",
  "sourceLastModifiedDateTime": "{{newSourceModifiedAt}}"
}

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 5.1
#
# A successful 200 has no JSON response body. Do not create a fake JSON file.

###############################################################################
# Part 5.2 - Verify the companion Registration rename
#
# Expected: 200 with unchanged IDs, source, owners, and the new displayName.

# @name renameGetRegistrationAfterNameSync
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/beta/copilot/agentRegistrations/{{companionRegistrationIdPath}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json
OData-Version: 4.0

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 5.2
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/companion-registration-after-name-sync.json
#
# Confirm every ID and owner matches companion-registration-before-rename.json.
# Then run:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py

###############################################################################
# Part 6.1 - Observe the companion Package name
#
# Expected: 200. The companion Package is an observation, not a PATCH target.
# Do not assume the Registration name propagates immediately.

# @name renameGetCompanionPackageAfterNameSync
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages/{{companionPackageId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 6.1
#
# Save:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/companion-package-after-name-sync.json
#
# If the old name remains, wait the agreed propagation period and retry only
# this GET. Do not PATCH the Package and do not repeat the Registration PATCH.
# Run prepare_rename.py after every saved observation.

###############################################################################
# Part 6.2 - Refresh inventory after all name updates
#
# Expected: 200. This catches a changed Package ID or duplicate record.

# @name renameListPackagesFinal
GET {{graphBaseUrl}}/v1.0/copilot/admin/catalog/packages
Authorization: Bearer {{renameToken.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json

###

###############################################################################
# REQUIRED AFTER PART 6.2
#
# 1. Save the first page:
# ../../evidence/demos/02-rename-companion/package-list-after-name-sync-page-1.json
# 2. Save every linked page as page-2.json, page-3.json, and so on.
# 3. Require one provider Package and one companion Package for the mapping.
# 4. Run:
# python demos/02-rename-companion/prepare_rename.py
#
# The final nameSyncStatus is in-sync only when every in-scope name matches.
# Any mismatch remains pending. An unavailable or unauthorized required update
# is blocked. Never delete and recreate an object to repair a display name.

###############################################################################
# Cleanup - restore names only after restoring the provider name
#
# To return the disposable experiment to its original names:
# 1. Rename the provider agent back through its supported provider interface.
# 2. Wait for healthy Registry Sync and prove the stable source key again.
# 3. Set A365_RENAME_NEW_TARGET_NAME to the original oldTargetName value.
# 4. Repeat Parts 3 through 6.
# 5. For shared mode, continue to skip Blueprint and principal rename.
# 6. Preserve the final rollback evidence and mapping; do not erase history.
